    <string name="legal_app_description_title">What OpenPage does</string>
    <string name="legal_app_description">OpenPage turns your phone into a direct printing and scanning station for USB printers. It connects over a USB-C or OTG adapter, renders documents on the phone, and speaks the printer’s own language — no drivers to install, no account, and no internet. Paper sizes, page ranges, margins, duplex, color and quality are all under your control.\n\nOpenPage includes built-in drivers for the major printer languages (PCL, ESC/P-R, ESC/POS, PostScript) and a conservative generic driver for models it doesn’t recognize.</string>
    <string name="about_company_title">The QAWSE Institute</string>
    <string name="about_company_blurb">The QAWSE Institute builds quiet, careful tools that respect the people using them. OpenPage is our printing and scanning instrument for everyone who just wants the page to come out right — without accounts, tracking or cloud dependencies.</string>
    <string name="legal_services_title">Services</string>
    <string name="legal_services">OpenPage provides document printing, page scanning (via printer glass or phone camera), page setup customization, and printer driver selection — all performed locally on your device.\n\nPrinting and scanning take place entirely over your USB connection. Donations are processed by PayPal on their own platform; OpenPage itself collects nothing.</string>
    <string name="legal_terms_title">Terms &amp; Conditions</string>
    <string name="legal_terms">By using OpenPage you agree to these terms.\n\nOpenPage is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. Printing and scanning depend on your hardware, cables and printer firmware; The QAWSE Institute cannot guarantee output on every model.\n\nYou remain responsible for the documents you print and scan, and for respecting the rights attached to them.\n\nOpenPage requests USB access solely to communicate with the printer or scanner you connect. It requests no other permissions and makes no network calls.\n\nThese terms are governed by the laws applicable in the developer’s jurisdiction, without prejudice to your statutory consumer rights.</string>
    <string name="legal_legal_title">Legal</string>
    <string name="legal_legal">OpenPage and its source artwork are the work of The QAWSE Institute. The OpenPage name and mark belong to their author.\n\nPrinter command languages referenced in the drivers (PCL, PostScript, ESC/POS, ESC/P-R, eSCL) are the properties of their respective owners and are implemented here as interoperable protocols, not affiliated products.\n\nNo Apple, Google, printer-manufacturer or other third-party trademarks are claimed. PayPal is used only via its public link and is not affiliated with OpenPage.</string>
